;; Tími NOW — DNS zone for timinow.pet
;;
;; Import: Cloudflare dashboard -> timinow.pet -> DNS -> Records -> Import and Export
;;         -> Import DNS records -> upload this file.
;;
;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;; READ THIS FIRST — Cloudflare imports every record as DNS-only (grey cloud).
;;
;; The six Worker records below MUST be switched to Proxied (orange cloud) after
;; import or the Workers will not answer on those hostnames. The Clerk records
;; below MUST stay DNS-only; proxying them breaks Clerk's Frontend API.
;;
;; A zone file cannot express proxy status, so this is a manual step either way.
;; `./scripts/check-dns.sh` verifies the result.
;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

$ORIGIN timinow.pet.
$TTL 300

;; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════ Cloudflare Workers ══
;;
;; 100:: is the IPv6 discard prefix. These records exist only so Cloudflare has
;; something to attach a Worker route to; no packet ever reaches that address.
;; Traffic is served by the Worker at the edge.
;;
;;   PROXIED (orange cloud) — all six.

@                       300  IN  AAAA   100::          ; -> timinow        (public site)
www                     300  IN  AAAA   100::          ; -> timinow        (same Worker)
app                     300  IN  AAAA   100::          ; -> timinow        (customer app)
providers               300  IN  AAAA   100::          ; -> timinow-vet    (veterinary console)
admin                   300  IN  AAAA   100::          ; -> timinow-admin  (platform operators)
voice                   300  IN  AAAA   100::          ; -> timinow-voice  (Twilio webhooks)

;; ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Clerk ══
;;
;; Authentication. Every target below is INSTANCE-SPECIFIC — replace
;; <instance> with the value Clerk shows under Domains in your production
;; instance. Clerk will not verify the domain until these resolve.
;;
;;   DNS-ONLY (grey cloud) — all five. Proxying these breaks sign-in.

clerk                   300  IN  CNAME  frontend-api.clerk.services.
accounts                300  IN  CNAME  accounts.clerk.services.

;; The three below are what let one-time codes arrive from timinow.pet rather
;; than from a Clerk address a veterinary practice will not recognise.
;;
;; They are COMMENTED OUT on purpose: their targets contain an instance id that
;; only your Clerk dashboard knows, and importing them with a placeholder would
;; create three broken records. Clerk shows the exact values under
;; Domains -> DNS records. Uncomment, substitute, and import again — or just add
;; those three by hand, which is usually quicker.
;;
;; clkmail              300  IN  CNAME  mail.<instance>.clerk.services.
;; clk._domainkey       300  IN  CNAME  dkim1.<instance>.clerk.services.
;; clk2._domainkey      300  IN  CNAME  dkim2.<instance>.clerk.services.

;; ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ Email ══
;;
;; Nothing sends mail from the apex today — the app's own addresses are on
;; clearkey.solutions, and Clerk sends from the clkmail subdomain above, which
;; Clerk's own records authenticate.
;;
;; So the apex publishes a hard SPF fail. On a domain nobody sends from, that is
;; free anti-spoofing: it stops someone forging billing@timinow.pet at a clinic.
;; If you later add Google Workspace or another sender, replace this line — see
;; dns/README.md.

@                       300  IN  TXT    "v=spf1 -all"

;; DMARC starts at p=none deliberately. Jumping straight to reject without ever
;; reading a report is how legitimate mail silently disappears. Watch the
;; reports for a fortnight, then tighten to quarantine and then reject.
_dmarc                  300  IN  TXT    "v=DMARC1; p=none; rua=mailto:1morecruise@gmail.com; ruf=mailto:1morecruise@gmail.com; fo=1; adkim=r; aspf=r; pct=100"

;; No inbound mail. Delete this and add MX records if you ever want a mailbox
;; at timinow.pet; the null MX is what tells senders not to bother trying.
@                       300  IN  MX     0 .

;; ═══════════════════════════════════════════════ Certificate authority ══
;;
;; Only these CAs may issue for timinow.pet. Cloudflare Universal SSL uses
;; Google Trust Services and Let's Encrypt; Clerk uses Let's Encrypt. The rest
;; are here so a future vendor does not fail issuance mysteriously — remove any
;; you are confident you will never use.

@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "pki.goog"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "letsencrypt.org"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "digicert.com"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "sectigo.com"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issue "ssl.com"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issuewild "pki.goog"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 issuewild "letsencrypt.org"
@                       300  IN  CAA    0 iodef "mailto:1morecruise@gmail.com"
